@tradition sunday-table
// The Sunday long table (weekly, seat 15). The plan's "Sunday roast", renamed: Sunday dinner is already the dish the
// crew voted for (section 17's menu), which isn't always a roast. The mess tables are pushed into long tables and
// friends sit together; Wednesday's tasting winner comes back as a side. A meal tradition:
// Design note: plans/trad-notes-weekly.md.
k: 440
title: Sunday long table
when: weekly sunday
at: 18:00-19:00
min: 30
jitter: 10
where: 3 room Mess hall: mess-seat
where: 3 room Mess hall: @long-table
where: 3 room Promenade: @long-table
hold: none
who: brennan always, lingers-at-meals 85%, everyone 60%
anim: talk
host: brennan
from: brennan
ties: galley meal=dinner seating=friends side=tasting
ties: decor longTables

meal: dinner
== mail
- Sunday long table tomorrow at {time}: the tables pushed together, the dish you voted for, and Wednesday's tasting winner on the side. Sit with your people.   #warm

== ask
- Long table tonight. Save me a seat?   #warm
- Sunday dinner at six. I voted for the curry. Again.   #funny
- Long table at six. Come and sit with us.   #warm

== here
- Pass that down, would you?
- Who voted for this? Whoever it was, thank you.   #funny
- Budge up, there's room for one more.   #warm

== thanks
- You squeeze in at the long table. A plate comes down the line to you without anyone asking.   #warm
- You sit down at the Sunday long table. Somebody tells a story you've heard before, and it's funnier this time.   #funny

== chatter
- Sunday long table is the one meal I never eat on my own.   #warm
- Someone always ends up at the wrong end of the long table from the gravy.   #funny
- Best seat at the long table is the middle. You hear everything.
